  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Lakhmi Chand vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 24 August, 2023 Author: Prem Narayan Singh",
    "facts": "Also heard on I.A. No. 12854/2023, which is an application filed under Section 397 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 for suspension of jail sentence and grant of bail on behalf of applicant.",
    "arguments": "5 . Learned counsel for the applicant submitted that the Courts below have not properly appreciated the oral and documentary evidence available on record and committed error in convicting the applicant. The samples of food which was collected by the Food Inspectors were in polythene bags, whereas the Rule of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 prescribes that the samples should always be collected in containers, jars or bottles. This revision would take considerable long time to dispose of finally.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5 . Learned counsel for the applicant submitted that the Courts below have not properly appreciated the oral and documentary evidence available on record and committed error in convicting the applicant. The samples of food which was collected by the Food Inspectors were in polythene bags, whereas the Rule of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 prescribes that the samples should always be collected in containers, jars or bottles. This revision would take considerable long time to dispose of finally.",
